Read AGENTS.md and MEDHA_STYLE.md first.

Add a <workspace | website | auth> page called "<page name>" at `<route, e.g. /dashboard/reports>`.

What the page shows:
- <section 1, e.g. a row of four metrics: …>
- <section 2, e.g. a table of … with columns …>

Requirements:
- Create `src/pages/<PageName>Page.tsx` using `AppShell` (workspace), `SiteShell` (website) or
  `AuthShell` (auth). Start with `PageHeading`, then `Panel`s in Bootstrap grid rows.
- Find the closest existing markup in `src/medha/pages/` (see `src/medha/CATALOG.md`) and reuse
  its class names instead of inventing new styles.
- Register the route in `src/App.tsx`; for a workspace page add a sidebar link in
  `src/medha/chrome/Sidebar.tsx`.
- Use typed props and sample data in a separate `const`, ready to be replaced by an API call.
- Add a test next to the page that renders it at its route.
- Run `{{ runScript }} lint`, `{{ runScript }} typecheck`, `{{ runScript }} check:style`,
  `{{ runScript }} test` and `{{ runScript }} build`, and report the results.
